            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>Methods, systems and apparatus for a monitoring system (100) including a plurality of dispensers (104) each configured to be located in a washroom and dispense a respective consumable hygiene product through a dispense cycle, where each of the dispensers (104) is associated with a water source device (105, 107); a water flow measurement device (109) configured to measure water flow to the water source devices (105, 107); and a data processing apparatus (102) configured to receive indications of dispense cycles from the dispensers (104), to receive a water flow measurement from the water flow measurement device (109), determine which water source device (105, 107) was active by associating one of the water source devices (105. 107) with one of the dispensers (104) based on a first time of the dispense cycle of the one of the dispensers (104) and a second time of the water flow measurement and determine a water flow fault of the one of the water source devices (105, 107) based on the first and second times.</p>
            </abstract>
